S3 Versioning in AWS
-----------------------
Versioning in Amazon S3 is a feature that keeps multiple versions of the same object in an S3 bucket.

It helps protect your files from accidental deletion or accidental overwrite.

-------or------------

S3 Versioning = keeping multiple versions of an object so that you can recover from accidental changes or deletions.


Example
--------
Suppose you upload: index.html

Initially: index.html → Version 1

Then you modify it and upload again: index.html → Version 2

S3 keeps both:
S3 Bucket
│
└── index.html
      ├── Version 1
      └── Version 2  ← Current version

So if you accidentally overwrite index.html, you can restore the previous version.


How to Enable Versioning
---------------------------
Go to: S3 → Bucket → Properties → Bucket Versioning → Edit
Select: Enable


